# Reference-tool and interop-image pins for the go-radx conformance and interop gates.
#
# This is the single human-readable manifest of every external reference tool and container image the
# gates depend on, recorded so an interop or conformance result is reproducible rather than dependent
# on whatever a runner resolves at install time. The pins themselves live next to where each tool is
# invoked — this file is the index and the rationale, and tools/pin-drift.sh asserts none of the live
# references float back to an unpinned tag.
#
# Format: one `key=value` per line; `#` starts a comment. Keys are lowercase, dot-separated.
# Bumping any pin is a deliberate, reviewed change: re-resolve the version/digest, update the live
# reference (the file noted under each entry), and update this manifest in the same commit.

# --- Go toolchain and scanners (live pins owned by P0-7; recorded here for one-stop visibility) ---
# go: mise.toml [tools], both go.mod files, ci.yml govulncheck job.
go=1.26.4
# golangci-lint: mise.toml [tools].
golangci-lint=2.12.2
# govulncheck: ci.yml `go install golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@vX.Y.Z`.
govulncheck=1.3.0

# --- DICOM conformance tools (live pins in .github/workflows/ci.yml, conformance job) ---
# dicom3tools provides dciodvfy. Pinned to the exact Ubuntu noble archive version via apt; apt has no
# point-in-time snapshot, so if the runner rolls the package forward the install fails loudly (the
# intended re-pin signal). Re-resolve with `apt-cache policy dicom3tools`.
dicom3tools=1.00~20240118131615-1
# pydicom round-trip gate. 3.x is required: the gate uses save_as(enforce_file_format=...), a 3.0 API.
pydicom=3.0.2

# --- Interop container images (live pins in the testcontainers helpers; digest-pinned) ---
# Orthanc: dimse/integration/orthanc/orthanc.go and dicomweb/integration/orthanc/orthanc.go.
orthanc.image=orthancteam/orthanc:26.6.0
orthanc.digest=sha256:510ef4ce24699104244b00d2b93350a801fc2f1c6b0bfc6a1f15e546bff2d1f4
# dcm4chee-arc three-container stack: dimse/integration/dcm4chee/dcm4chee.go.
dcm4chee.slapd.image=dcm4che/slapd-dcm4chee:2.6.10-34.2
dcm4chee.slapd.digest=sha256:5c04ced61e943af2175c69ec7955c28bbaf676c50b5876c02e1437261cfaeefc
dcm4chee.postgres.image=dcm4che/postgres-dcm4chee:17.4-34
dcm4chee.postgres.digest=sha256:728c3055b894127c661a1645ffd0ccc2ad6461b86e957e245a9cc9bbc9c499e2
dcm4chee.arc.image=dcm4che/dcm4chee-arc-psql:5.34.2
dcm4chee.arc.digest=sha256:316eba283d3c8538e4c3b954edcdd59572f76aa7271ca6336ddf771703082f8c

# --- FHIR validator (mechanism pin; not invoked in CI until Phase 1 / M6a) ---
# Mechanism decision: the official HL7 validator_cli.jar (hapifhir/org.hl7.fhir.core releases), NOT a
# container. Rationale: the jar is the canonical reference, runs on the JDK every runner can install,
# pins to a single immutable GitHub release asset, and avoids a second container registry dependency.
# When the M6a gate is wired (a tools/fhir-conformance/ runner), it must download exactly this release
# asset and verify it before use; record the asset SHA-256 here at that time.
fhir-validator.mechanism=validator_cli.jar
fhir-validator.source=https://github.com/hapifhir/org.hl7.fhir.core/releases/tag/6.9.9
fhir-validator.version=6.9.9

# --- Python reference libraries (parity/shape references; not installed by any current gate) ---
# Recorded for the determinism contract: if a future gate installs either, it must pin the version
# here and at the install site, and tools/pin-drift.sh will require a pinned `==` / git ref.
# python-hl7 publishes on PyPI under the distribution name `hl7` (so `pip install hl7==0.4.5`).
pynetdicom=3.0.4
python-hl7=0.4.5
